@startuml "Status Push & Staleness Watchdog"

!theme cerulean
title Status Push & Staleness Watchdog

participant "DJI Camera" as DJI
participant "OsmoBLEConnection" as BLE
participant "OsmoCamera" as Cam
participant "OsmoCameraManager" as Mgr
participant "UI Views" as UI

== Status Push (1 Hz from Camera) ==

loop every ~1 second
  DJI -> BLE : BLE Notify ← 0xFFF4\n  CmdSet=0x1D, CmdID=0x02\n  (push, not response)

  BLE -> Cam : AsyncStream yields data

  Cam -> Cam : FrameParser.parse()
  Cam -> Cam : IncomingFrame:\n  isPush == true\n  cmdSet=0x1D, cmdID=0x02

  Cam -> Cam : CameraStatus.parse(\n  payload: 38 bytes)

  note right of Cam
    Payload layout:
    [0]    rawMode
    [1]    recordingStatus
    [5-6]  recordingSeconds (LE)
    [28]   powerMode
    [37]   batteryPercentage
    + resolution, fps, ratio,
      stabilization, storage, etc.
  end note

  Cam -> Cam : status = parsed status
  Cam -> Cam : lastSeenDate = Date.now

  Cam -> UI : @Observable triggers\n  view re-render
end

== Staleness Watchdog (1 Hz tick) ==

loop every 1 second
  Mgr -> Mgr : checkStaleness()

  loop each enabled connected camera
    Mgr -> Cam : Check lastSeenDate

    alt now - lastSeenDate > stalenessTimeout (default 5s)
      alt camera has commands in flight
        note right of Mgr
          Skip staleness check:
          camera may pause status
          during mode switch or
          other operations
        end note
      else no commands in flight
        Mgr -> Cam : forceDisconnect()
        Mgr -> Cam : clearStatus()
        Mgr -> Cam : connectionState = .reconnecting
        Mgr -> Mgr : scheduleReconnect(camera)
      end
    end
  end

  note right of Mgr
    Also checks for stuck passive
    reconnects (>30s in .reconnecting
    with no peripheral connection).
    Kicks these by cancelling and
    re-issuing CB connect.
  end note
end

== Stale Continuation Reaping ==

note over Cam
  Opportunistic cleanup piggybacked
  on sendAndWait() calls:

  Any pendingResponse or
  pendingCommandWaiter older than
  30 seconds is failed with timeout
  error and removed.
end note

@enduml
